docs/VALIDATION.md:180: - When asserting the end state of a CSS transition or animation in a headless browser, emulate `prefers-reduced-motion` (or otherwise disable animations) and assert the computed end state, rather than sampling after a wall-clock delay; headless browsers may throttle frame updates while other animations run, making timing-based checks flaky. Verify animated states separately via the reduced-motion code path or an explicit animation-disable override, and record that as the method used.
